Kubernetes DaemonSets: Running Pods on Every Node

A DaemonSet ensures that a copy of a pod runs on all (or selected) nodes in your cluster. When you add a new node, the DaemonSet automatically schedules a pod there too.

Why Use DaemonSets?
- Deploying monitoring agents (e.g., Prometheus Node Exporter)
- Running logging agents (e.g., Fluentd, Filebeat)
- Networking components (e.g., CNI plugins)

Key Benefit: Simplifies cluster-wide workloads that must exist everywhere.
